// A global shared between an ISR (via the inc_count helper) and main must be
// volatile, and the ISR must not do a non-atomic read-modify-write on it. Both
// rules are enforced TRANSITIVELY through the helper call (ISR-TRANS fix) —
// pre-fix the non-volatile / RMW form compiled silently and hoisted/torn on real
// hardware.
//
// BUG-788 (2026-08-14): this file used to increment with
// `irq_count = irq_count + 1`, believing that to be the safe alternative to
// `irq_count += 1`. It is not — both lower to the same load/add/store, and an
// interrupt landing between the load and the store loses the count. The old
// diagnostic's advice ("use explicit read/mask/write") is what led this test to
// the racy form, which is precisely why the RMW rule now asks whether the
// right-hand side READS the object rather than looking for a `+=` token.
//
// The genuinely correct increment is atomic.
volatile u32 irq_count = 0;
void inc_count() { @atomic_add(&irq_count, 1); }
interrupt USART1 {
    inc_count();
}
